+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html lang="en">
+<head>
+<meta charset="utf-8">
+<link rel="stylesheet" href="/reaper/reaper_cb.css"><script>/*REAPER-CBMODE*/if(<% nvram_get_js("reaper_cbmode"); %>==="1")document.documentElement.classList.add("cb");</script>
+<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
+<meta name="reaper-native" content="1">
+<title>REAPER &mdash; Time Machine</title>
+<!-- Reaper_TimeMachine.asp - USB Application > Time Machine (Reaper-native UI, 2026-11-25).
+     Replaces Advanced_TimeMachine.asp: the same settings (timemachine_enable, tm_device_name, tm_vol_size)
+     and the same service (restart_timemachine), parity file build-scripts/tests/ui_parity/Advanced_TimeMachine.json.
+     Kept from stock: the size is typed in GB and stored in MB (0 = no limit), it may not exceed the free space
+     of the chosen partition, a partition with 1 GB free or less cannot be chosen, choosing another partition
+     clears the size, and tm_ui_setting=1 rides with every save (rc/timemachine.c takes the page's partition
+     only then). Differences, on purpose: the partition is a menu on the page (stock opened a panel);
+     the two FAQ links are not carried (they went through an ASUS forwarding address). -->
+<link rel="stylesheet" href="/reaper/rp.css">
+<style>
+/* page-specific rules only; the Reaper look comes from /reaper/rp.css */
